<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duke Wen of Qin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 716 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Duke Wen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-qin">State of Qin</a> from 765 to 716 BCE. He defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rong-people">Rong peoples</a> and took the lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-qi">Mount Qi</a>, the old Zhou heartland in the Wei valley, gathering the Zhou population that remained there. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/records-of-the-grand-historian">Shiji</a> credits him with appointing historians to keep records and with introducing harsher punishments, steps in Qin's growth into an organised state.</p></div>
